From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rolando Trevino <rolotrealanis@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 19:29:32 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] drm/apple: say why a T6050 DCP is not started

dcp_check_firmware_version() refuses a T6050 DCP whose
apple,firmware-compat is not 27.0.0 without a word: the probe ends in
-ENODEV and the boot framebuffer stays, but nothing says why. Log the
compat it refused, as the T6041 and T6030 paths do, and the firmware
version it accepted.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Rolando Trevino <rolotrealanis@gmail.com>

---
 drivers/gpu/drm/apple/dcp.c | 8 +++++++-
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/dcp.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/dcp.c
index 6b464c1e5d31..82e2eb0c1439 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/dcp.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/dcp.c
@@ -4939,8 +4939,14 @@ static enum dcp_firmware_version dcp_check_firmware_version(struct device *dev)
 
 	if (hw->firmware_compat == DCP_FIRMWARE_V_27_0) {
 		ret = dcp_read_fw_version(dev, "apple,firmware-compat", compat_str);
-		if (ret < 0 || strcmp(compat_str, "27.0.0"))
+		if (ret < 0 || strcmp(compat_str, "27.0.0")) {
+			dev_err(dev, "T6050 display not started: DCP firmware-compat %s is not 27.0.0\n",
+				ret < 0 ? "missing" : compat_str);
 			return DCP_FIRMWARE_UNKNOWN;
+		}
+		ret = dcp_read_fw_version(dev, "apple,firmware-version", fw_str);
+		dev_info(dev, "DCP firmware-compat 27.0.0 (FW: %s)\n",
+			 ret < 0 ? "missing" : fw_str);
 		return DCP_FIRMWARE_V_27_0;
 	}
 
